# 1. Process Management and System Health

## Process Monitoring

Useful commands:

```bash
ps
ps -A
ps aux
top
uptime
```

### Purpose

- View running processes
- Monitor CPU and Memory usage
- Check Load Average
- Identify Process IDs (PID)

### Process Management

```bash
kill <PID>
kill -9 <PID>
pkill <process_name>
pgrep <process_name>
```

---

# 2. Advanced Grep

### Case-insensitive Search

```bash
grep -i "error" file.log
```

### Inverted Search

```bash
grep -v "running" pods.txt
```

### Multiple Pattern Search

```bash
grep -E "error|failed" app.log
```

### Recursive Search

```bash
grep -r "password" /etc
```

### Whole Word Search

```bash
grep -w "root" /etc/passwd
```

### Count Matching Lines

```bash
grep "ERROR" app.log | wc -l
```

