# 4. Shell Scripting

## Shebang

```bash
#!/bin/bash
```

Specifies the shell interpreter.

---

## Special Variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `$?` | Exit status of previous command |
| `$$` | Current Shell PID |
| `$!` | Last Background Process PID |
| `$0` | Current Script Name |

Example:

```bash
ls

echo $?
```

