# 6. Cron Jobs

## Edit Cron

```bash
crontab -e
```

## List Cron Jobs

```bash
crontab -l
```

## Remove Cron Jobs

```bash
crontab -r
```

### Cron Format

```
* * * * *
- - - - -
| | | | |
| | | | +---- Day of Week
| | | +------ Month
| | +-------- Day of Month
| +---------- Hour
+------------ Minute
```

Example:

```bash
0 2 * * * /home/ubuntu/backup.sh
```

Runs daily at **2:00 AM**.

